.nh
.TH "SHELLY" "1" "Oct 2026" "Shelly CLI" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
shelly-audit - Security audit for devices


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBshelly audit [device...] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Perform a security audit on Shelly devices.

.PP
Checks performed:
  - auth:     Authentication status (password protection)
  - cloud:    Cloud connection exposure (cloud connected without a password)
  - firmware: Firmware version (security patches)

.PP
Every check runs by default. Pass one or more --check- flags to run
only those checks.

.PP
With no device named, every registered device is audited (the same as --all).

.PP
Use -o json or -o yaml for one structured result per device, suitable for
scripting.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--all\fP[=false]
	Audit all registered devices (the default when no device is named)

.PP
\fB--check-auth\fP[=false]
	Check authentication (password protection)

.PP
\fB--check-cloud\fP[=false]
	Check cloud connection exposure

.PP
\fB--check-firmware\fP[=false]
	Check for firmware updates

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for audit


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	Config file (default $HOME/.config/shelly/config.yaml)

.PP
\fB-F\fP, \fB--fields\fP[=false]
	Print available field names for use with --jq and --template

.PP
\fB-Q\fP, \fB--jq\fP=[]
	Apply jq expression to filter output (repeatable, joined with |)

.PP
\fB--log-categories\fP=""
	Filter logs by category (comma-separated: network,api,device,config,auth,plugin)

.PP
\fB--log-json\fP[=false]
	Output logs in JSON format

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	Disable colored output

.PP
\fB--no-headers\fP[=false]
	Hide table headers in output

.PP
\fB--offline\fP[=false]
	Only read from cache, error on cache miss

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="table"
	Output format (table, json, yaml, template)

.PP
\fB--plain\fP[=false]
	Disable borders and colors (machine-readable output)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Suppress non-essential output

.PP
\fB--raw\fP[=false]
	Print the exact device response(s) as a JSON array and suppress normal output

.PP
\fB--refresh\fP[=false]
	Bypass cache and fetch fresh data from device

.PP
\fB--template\fP=""
	Go template string for output (use with -o template)

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	Increase verbosity (-v=info, -vv=debug, -vvv=trace)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  # Audit a single device
  shelly audit kitchen-light

  # Audit multiple devices
  shelly audit light-1 switch-2

  # Audit all registered devices
  shelly audit

  # Only check firmware and authentication, as JSON
  shelly audit --check-firmware --check-auth -o json

  # Only check cloud exposure on one device
  shelly audit kitchen-light --check-cloud
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBshelly(1)\fP
